00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:16.810
So the best way is to optimize
this by keeping workers safe,

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.930
and avoid costly shutdowns,
and prevent disruptions.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.810
So again, maintenance is key.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.630
So having established
that, we did

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:29.560
some study of various analysts
and various industry bodies,

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.630
and this is what they found.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:34.930
About 40% of preventive
maintenance costs

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:40.940
are spent on assets with
negligible impact on uptime.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:44.580
30% of preventive maintenance
are carried out too frequently,

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:45.680
which are not needed.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.700
And 45% of maintenance
efforts are ineffective.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.520
What does this tell us?

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:59.940
This tells us that
time-based approach is not

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.840
going to work for the future.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.130
And we need a
condition-based monitoring.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.730
And at the same
time, as we know,

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.180
there are components
which talk to each other.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.780
We need to be able
to harness that data

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:17.070
and have the ability to
not only store, but also

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:20.270
analyze the data on the edge.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.640
So to summarize the
business benefits

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.200
of predictive
maintenance, I think

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.930
we've established different
