00:34:50.139 --> 00:34:52.409
What's in the future?

00:34:52.409 --> 00:34:57.000
As we think about the future, we
can talk about a lot of things

00:34:57.000 --> 00:34:59.890
that we can do with
IoT and ML together,

00:34:59.890 --> 00:35:03.900
whether it is in the area
of manufacturing, domain

00:35:03.900 --> 00:35:08.910
of manufacturing, or putting
automation, robotics,

00:35:08.910 --> 00:35:12.030
or whether it's transforming
service industry

00:35:12.030 --> 00:35:15.390
or building smarter
cities, as Mike alluded to.

00:35:15.390 --> 00:35:20.230
So I'll throw some light
on a couple of these cases,

00:35:20.230 --> 00:35:24.510
and then we'll have some
time for Q&amp;A towards the end.

00:35:24.510 --> 00:35:27.475
So just take an example
of the service industry.

00:35:30.650 --> 00:35:34.330
Using the concepts that
we have talked about--

00:35:34.330 --> 00:35:37.700
predictive maintenance,
IoT, and ML--

00:35:37.700 --> 00:35:39.360
they can be different
business models.

00:35:39.360 --> 00:35:41.790
So one of them is
asset as a service.

00:35:41.790 --> 00:35:49.450
So instead of selling equipment,
you're just offering capacity.

00:35:49.450 --> 00:35:52.350
Just as the software is a
service, asset is a service.

00:35:52.350 --> 00:35:55.860
And where you are able to
predict time to failure,

00:35:55.860 --> 00:36:00.900
you are able to find whether
the machine has degraded,

00:36:00.900 --> 00:36:02.220
find anomalies there.

00:36:02.220 --> 00:36:07.560
And thereby you can improve the
profitability of your warranty

00:36:07.560 --> 00:36:08.430
deals.

00:36:08.430 --> 00:36:12.450
Like there are companies
which specialize in this.

00:36:12.450 --> 00:36:15.930
Now this has also
an added advantage

00:36:15.930 --> 00:36:22.770
of moving from capex to opex,
and the financial CFOs actually

00:36:22.770 --> 00:36:28.000
love this concept whereby
you are able to capitalize.

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.710
Another model is the
usage based insurance.

00:36:31.710 --> 00:36:35.730
Now this is where the behavior
of the driver comes in handy.

00:36:35.730 --> 00:36:38.820
If you are able to track by
putting a special device,

00:36:38.820 --> 00:36:41.580
like what Geotab has.

00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:47.430
Those devices have ability
to-- they are sensors,

00:36:47.430 --> 00:36:50.440
and they have the
ability to not only store

00:36:50.440 --> 00:36:51.930
the various parameters.

00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:59.619
They can find out if the
driver was rash, if there

00:36:59.619 --> 00:37:00.910
were some potholes on the road.

00:37:00.910 --> 00:37:07.730
So all of that can be
used to either incentivize

00:37:07.730 --> 00:37:10.920
a particular set of users
in a particular zip code.

00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:12.780
And obviously there
are privacy concerns,

00:37:12.780 --> 00:37:16.860
so a lot of this thing is
generalized and offered

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:19.380
as a different model.

00:37:19.380 --> 00:37:21.240
And this pricing
model is actually

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:23.740
disrupting the
insurance industry.

00:37:23.740 --> 00:37:27.090
Another example in
the service industry

00:37:27.090 --> 00:37:28.590
is benchmarking as a service.

00:37:28.590 --> 00:37:30.570
So obviously when
you are collecting

00:37:30.570 --> 00:37:31.620
all this kind of data--

00:37:31.620 --> 00:37:35.340
reliability data from products
where the sensors are talking,

00:37:35.340 --> 00:37:39.720
and how you are
consolidating feedback

00:37:39.720 --> 00:37:41.760
to the product manufacturers.

00:37:41.760 --> 00:37:45.334
And this data and
predictive insights

00:37:45.334 --> 00:37:47.250
can be provided to others
in the same industry

00:37:47.250 --> 00:37:50.040
